      "text": "every woman shall borrow of her neighbour, Ex. 3:22. every man borrow of his neighbour, Ex. 11:2 (12:35). if a man borrow ought of his neighbour, Ex. 22:14. thou shalt lend … but thou shalt not borrow, Deut. 15:6 (28:12). Alas, master! for it was borrowed, 2 Kgs. 6:5 (6:1–7). borrowed money for the king’s tribute, Neh. 5:4. wicked borroweth, and payeth not, Ps. 37:21. the borrower is servant to the lender, Prov. 22:7.",
